title: "Lean LFM-to-Dirac Derivation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Partin"
    given-names: "G. D."
version: "0.15.0-research"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpartin/LeanDiracDerivation"
license: CC0-1.0
abstract: >-
  A noncanonical Lean 4 research derivation through DIRAC-015. It connects a
  positive two-field C19 action to a massive C19 Klein-Gordon tangent and
  proves that a cubical four-component Dirac Hamiltonian squares to its
  continuum symbol. It controls lattice/time corrections and derives the
  positive-frequency density/current limit from the same action. A localized
  physical electron, electromagnetic coupling, and uniqueness remain open.
